        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-06T15:37:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the independent features are represented by `libhyp` as distinct traits and we support having none, one or the other, or both.\n\nThis `match` assumes what KVM currently provides: a \"regular\" API (no MMIO_GUARD, no MEM_SHARE) and a \"protected\" one (has both), whereas the other 2 combinations aren\u0027t supported. Differentiating between them is done in a best effort approach while avoiding to validate the whole API at constructor-time. If a call is missing (say this `match` concludes that this it\u0027s running pKVM but MMIO_GUARD isn\u0027t actually implemented), it will fail and be reported at the call site.",
      "parentUuid": "31810867_28584caa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 64,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 64,
        "endChar": 81
      },
